{
  "_comment": [
    "CANONICAL catalog parser rules — the single source of truth.",
    "app/assets/catalog/parsers.json is GENERATED from this file by",
    "tools/gen_catalog_assets.py; tools/ci_gates.sh fails CI when they diverge.",
    "Edit here, regenerate, never hand-edit the asset.",
    "Amount scale is {1,3} per migration 0091 (2- and 3-decimal currencies).",
    "",
    "SNB (...101) — BILINGUAL AMOUNT GRAMMAR.",
    "The amount must be ADJACENT to a currency token, on either side:",
    "  Arabic   'مبلغ:SAR 45.00'   currency BEFORE  (lookbehind)",
    "  English  'Amount 8 SAR'     currency AFTER   (lookahead)",
    "Both are zero-width assertions, so the captured token is unchanged.",
    "WHY: with the currency optional the lazy [\\s\\S]*? let the amount group take",
    "the FIRST digit run after the keyword, which on the real layout is the masked",
    "card number. Reproduced as 4521 instead of 45.00 against the anonymized",
    "fixture known_bank_known_merchant_auto_confirm and on real-holdout records.",
    "An earlier fix required the currency BEFORE the amount only, which silently",
    "broke the English layout; this grammar covers both without widening to",
    "'nearest number' — a digit run with no adjacent currency (card suffix,",
    "account suffix, reference, date, time) can never be captured.",
    "",
    "Riyad (...103): UNCHANGED. Same pattern shape, but the defect could not be",
    "reproduced on any available Riyad message. Its real layout is",
    "'مبلغ:700.00 SAR'. Tracked as an open risk: the card line precedes the",
    "amount line, so a Riyad message carrying a لدى/At anchor would capture the",
    "card suffix. Requires bank-sourced evidence before changing a money rule.",
    "",
    "FIELD OWNERSHIP — canonical vs database-runtime.",
    "  CANONICAL-OWNED (generated into BOTH projections; CI fails on drift):",
    "    id                identity, stable, never regenerated",
    "    bank_id           identity; the DB projection ASSERTS it rather than",
    "                      rewriting it, so a mismatch fails loudly instead of",
    "                      silently re-pointing a rule at another bank",
    "    sender_pattern    configuration",
    "    message_pattern   configuration",
    "    transaction_type  configuration",
    "    language          configuration",
    "    priority          configuration",
    "    extracted_fields  configuration (the rule's extraction contract)",
    "  DB-RUNTIME-OWNED (excluded BY DESIGN, never generated):",
    "    is_active, is_deleted            operational state; an admin deactivates",
    "                                     or tombstones, and the device's authority",
    "                                     epoch decides activation from the served",
    "                                     snapshot. The bundle seeds INACTIVE",
    "                                     regardless of what this file carries.",
    "    created/updated/deleted_version  assigned by trg_parsers_version",
    "    created_at, updated_at           database lifecycle metadata",
    "    validation_status, validated_at, validated_by, golden_test_count,",
    "    false_positive_count, amount_error_count",
    "                                     evidence, written only by parser-test",
    "  is_active, is_deleted and updated_at appear in the bundled asset as SEED",
    "  DEFAULTS only \u2014 the three exceptions. The generator rejects any OTHER",
    "  runtime field on a canonical rule rather than dropping it silently.",
    "  Generating any runtime field would let a file overwrite state the database",
    "  owns; omitting a canonical field would let the bundle and the database",
    "  diverge, which is exactly what happened with 0091."
  ],
